.TH FS80HCTL 1 "November 2026" "fs80hctl 0.2.0" "fs80hctl User Manual"
.SH NAME
fs80hctl \- Technical acquisition, custody, and processing utility for Futronic FS80/FS80H scanners
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fs80hctl
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<text|json|raw>\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-vv\fR|\fB\-vvv\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENTS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fs80hctl
is a pure-Rust command-line tool for technical and forensic operations on
Futronic optical fingerprint scanners (FS80, FS80H, and FS81H). It provides direct
optical sensor acquisition, biometric standard compliance (500 DPI), image quality metrics,
format transcoding with immutable chain of custody, and deterministic 1:1 biometric comparison.
It also provides technical forensic analysis and image tools; these results are
not identification decisions, expert reports, or certified PAD claims.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fI<text|json|raw>\fR
Output format mode: text (human-readable), json (structured JSON payload), or raw (pure byte stream to stdout).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Shorthand alias for --format json. Output results in structured JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase logging verbosity on stderr (-v for INFO, -vv for DEBUG, -vvv for TRACE).
.TP
.BR \-\-mock " " \fI<match|mismatch|degraded|empty|disconnect>\fR
Simulated hardware mock scenario for testing without physical scanner. Also configurable via FS80H_MOCK_FIXTURE environment variable.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and syntax.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print installed program version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Run environment diagnostics: USB subsystem, device access permissions, udev rules (Linux), user groups, external NFIQ2 availability, and filesystem write.
.TP
.B devices
List connected Futronic fingerprint scanners on the USB bus.
.TP
.B device inspect [\-\-bus N] [\-\-address N]
Open and inspect USB communication with the specified scanner.
.TP
.B capture [\-o FILE] [\-\-image\-format FORMAT] [\-\-raw] [\-\-wait] [\-\-timeout SECS] [\-\-min\-quality SCORE]
Acquire an optical biometric frame (320x480, 500 DPI) and write the custody manifest (.meta.json). Use \-\-wait for auto-trigger when the finger contact stabilizes. With global \-\-format raw, streams raw 153,600 bytes to stdout.
.TP
.B enroll [\-o FILE] [\-\-samples N] [\-\-timeout SECS] [\-\-min\-quality SCORE]
Acquire multiple samples consecutively and automatically elect and save the highest quality sample (best-of-N).
.TP
.B convert INPUT [\-t FORMAT] [\-o OUTPUT] [\-\-invert]
Transcode across formats (PNG, TIFF, PGM, RAW) while preserving chain of custody.
.TP
.B inspect IMAGE
Inspect metadata, SHA-256 hash, and quality metrics of a biometric image.
.TP
.B verify PROBE [REFERENCE] [\-\-gallery DIR] [\-\-threshold T] [\-\-exit\-code]
Compare biometric images (1:1 with reference file or 1:N against a gallery directory) and calculate technical similarity score.
.TP
.B template create|inspect|validate|convert|base64
Create, inspect, validate, convert, or explicitly Base64-transport fingerprint minutiae templates. Supported profiles are ISO/IEC 19794-2:2005, ISO/IEC 19794-2:2011, ANSI INCITS 378:2004, ANSI INCITS 378:2009, and ANSI INCITS 378:2009/AM1. Template validation is structural and does not certify matching accuracy or PAD performance.
.TP
.B forensic annotate|compare|liveness|report
Run technical minutiae annotation, corroborated-pair comparison, static liveness screening, or a JSON-only forensic report. Comparison requires at least six geometrically consistent minutiae pairs before it may return a non-zero score. The liveness screen is a heuristic, not a certified presentation-attack-detection result. Keep real biometric inputs and all derived output outside the repository; see docs/FORENSIC_BIOMETRIC_VALIDATION.md.
.TP
.B tool enhance|convert|bench
Enhance a fingerprint image, convert RAW/PNG/WSQ interchange files, or run deterministic synthetic matching and image-I/O benchmarks.
.TP
.B serve [\-\-socket\-path PATH] [\-\-systemd]
Run background capture daemon over Unix Domain Socket for low-latency acquisition.
.TP
.B manual
Display technical reference manual and usage guide on standard output.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.TP
.B PNG
8-bit grayscale with calibrated pHYs chunk at 500 DPI.
.TP
.B TIFF
Baseline 6.0 with full EXIF tags and 500 DPI resolution.
.TP
.B PGM
Netpbm binary format P5 (NIST NBIS standard).
.TP
.B RAW
Uncompressed 153,600-byte raw pixel dump.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success / Biometric verification confirmed (Match).
.TP
.B 1
Operational error: syntax error, invalid parameters, or general failure.
.TP
.B 2
Biometric mismatch (comparison score below configured threshold).
.TP
.B 3
Capture timeout or finger not detected within acquisition window.
.TP
.B 4
Biometric quality insufficient (rejected by quality evaluation) or liveness score below the heuristic threshold.
.TP
.B 5
USB hardware failure (device not found, permission denied, I/O error).
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/MANUAL.md, README.md
